<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22683" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γοργόνειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γοργεῖος, πεδία</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				793
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ Γ.</span>”
				<i>a Gorgon-mask,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					IG
					2.654
				</span></i>
			,al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Them.</u>
				10
			</span></i>; <i>the Gorgon's head</i>, a group of stars in Perseus,
				<i><span class="en">
				Gem.
				3.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Alm.</u>
				7.5
			</span></i>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Them.</u>
				10
			</span></i>; but also, the constellation <u>Medusa</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Hipparch.
				2.3.27
			</span></i>, al.; <i>bogey</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
			</span></i>
			inc.<i><span class="en">
				20.27
			</span></i>; Orphic name for the <i>moon</i>, because of the face in
			it, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γ., τό,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιθόσπερμον</span>
			, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.141
			</span></i>.</div>
